<title>JAPAN: Nippon Credit shares surge.</title>
<headline>Nippon Credit shares surge.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Credit Bank Ltd (NCB) surged on Friday having earlier stood bid-only as investors rushed to buy back shares they had previously sold short, traders said.</p>
<p>The bank said on Thursday that it and Bankers Trust New York Corp had agreed on a business tie-up, encouraging traders who had sold off the shares to buy back, they said.</p>
<p>At 0150 GMT, the share was up 45 yen, or 23.68 percent, at 235. It was the steepest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The trade volume of 10.826 million shares was the heaviest on the first section.</p>
